## The page builder: derived, MIT

`src/resume_markdown/` is derived from mikepqr/resume-markdown by
Mike Lee Williams, https://github.com/mikepqr/resume-markdown, under the MIT
licence. His notice is `src/resume_markdown/LICENSE` and it stays with his
code, which is where it applies. Measured against upstream: 266 of his 267
lines survive verbatim -- the Chrome discovery, the PDF writer, the HTML
assembly and the command line are all his.

My additions to that file are structural. Markdown emits a flat list of
sibling elements, which is enough to style a document and not enough to ask
"the section the pointer is in" or "the position being read". It now wraps
each heading-led run in a section and each position in an article, marks date
lines by matching their text, numbers every unit in reading order for the
load-in sequence, links the profile handles on the contact line, and splits
labelled skill entries onto their own lines. All of it is presentation the
source file should not have to carry.

`src/resume_markdown/resume.md` and `resume.css` are his template files,
shipped so `resume-markdown init` still works. They are not my resume.

